ting.\"),\n  R(\"unexpected DB error\",\"enforced\",\"src/main.py:157\",\"except Exception as exc:\",\"Records run_error then re-raises; action not run.\")])\n# ---------- B07\ncheck(\"B07.1\",\"yes\",\"config/agent.yaml:18\",\"max_steps: 12\",\"All six limits have finite values in config and are enforced by RunBudget.\",\n counter=\"Searched for None/0/-1/inf limits and unbounded loops; while True at agent.py:65 calls check_step each pass. max_subagents: 0 means none allowed (budgets.py:67 raises when started >= 0).\",\n rows=[R(\"loop count\",\"enforced\",\"config/agent.yaml:18\",\"max_steps: 12\",\"check_step raises at budgets.py:31.\"),\n  R(\"run time\",\"enforced\",\"config/agent.yaml:19\",\"max_wall_seconds: 90\",\"check_step and per-call timeout.\"),\n  R(\"tokens\",\"enforced\",\"config/agent.yaml:20\",\"max_total_tokens: 60000\",\"check_step raises at budgets.py:35.\"),\n  R(\"cost\",\"enforced\",\"config/agent.yaml:21\",\"max_cost_usd: 0.40\",\"check_step raises at budgets.py:37.\"),\n  R(\"tool-call rate\",\"enforced\",\"config/agent.yaml:22\",\"max_tool_calls_per_minute: 20\",\"check_tool_call at budgets.py:62.\"),\n  R(\"sub-agents\",\"enforced\",\"config/agent.yaml:23\",\"max_subagents: 0\",\"check_subagent raises for any start.\")])\ncheck(\"B07.2\",\"no\",\"src/agent.py:154\",\"bal = await self.gateway.call(balance_spec,\",\n \"Resume path makes an extra get_leave_balance call that never passes check_tool_call; the Anthropic client also retries (main.py:172 max_retries=1) outside the counters; gateway_client direct-route fallback repeats a call uncounted. Token/cost are checked before a call, not reserved, so overshoot is one call.\")\ncheck(\"B07.3\",\"yes\",\"config/agent.yaml:23\",\"max_subagents: 0\",\"The agent has no sub-agent, spawn or handoff path and the cap is zero.\",\n counter=\"Searched src/, config/, prompts/ for spawn, subagent, handoff, Task, create_agent; only the cap, an unused counter (agent.py:40) and unused check_subagent exist.\",\n rows=[R(\"sub-agent spawn paths\",\"not_applicable\",\"config/agent.yaml:23\",\"max_subagents: 0\",\"No spawning code exists; cap of 0 refuses any start.\"),\n  R(\"nested spawn depth\",\"not_applicable\",\"src/budgets.py:67\",\"if started_so_far >= self.cfg[\\\"max_subagents\\\"]:\",\"With cap 0 no child or nested child can start.\")])\ncheck(\"B07.4\",\"no\",\"src/gateway.py:48\",\"_rate: dict[tuple[str, str], deque] = defaultdict(deque)\",\n \"Tool-call rate limits are per-replica in-process memory (two replicas), keyed per instance and subject only; no tenant or fleet rate quota. Spend quotas are checked only at run start (budgets.py:78) and charged after each call, so many concurrent runs can each spend up to the per-run cap: user $3/day with 150 runs of $0.40 is bounded only at $60.\")\n# ---------- B08\ncheck(\"B08.1\",\"yes\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:8\",\"policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]\",\n \"Namespace default-deny for ingress and egress; Cilium policies allow only named peers.\",\n counter=\"Searched all manifests for 0.0.0.0/0, broad CIDRs and allow-all rules; none.\",\n rows=[R(\"default deny\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:8\",\"policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]\",\"podSelector {} with no rules denies all.\"),\n  R(\"agent egress peers\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:37\",\"- toEndpoints:\",\"Only gateway, STS, postgres, otel, helpdesk-mcp and two FQDNs on named ports; helpdesk-mcp is a listed server (see B09.2 for its direct route).\"),\n  R(\"agent ingress\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:20\",\"- matchLabels: {\\\"k8s:io.kubernetes.pod.namespace\\\": web-frontends, app: hr-portal-bff}\",\"Only the portal BFF on 8080.\"),\n  R(\"gateway egress/ingress\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:77\",\"- matchLabels: {\\\"k8s:io.kubernetes.pod.namespace\\\": hris, app: hris-mcp}\",\"Gateway reaches hris-mcp, helpdesk-mcp, sts, postgres only.\")])\ncheck(\"B08.2\",\"yes\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:52\",\"- toCIDR: [169.254.169.254/32, 169.254.170.2/32, 100.100.100.200/32]\",\n \"No broad egress; cloud metadata v4 and v6 explicitly denied; no host mounts or host networking.\",\n counter=\"Searched deployment.yaml for hostNetwork, hostPath, docker.sock, privileged; none. Secrets are the agent's own DB and API key; DB role is limited (migrations:83-85).\",\n rows=[R(\"egress routes\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:52\",\"- toCIDR: [169.254.169.254/32, 169.254.170.2/32, 100.100.100.200/32]\",\"Metadata IPv4 blocked.\"),\n  R(\"IPv6 metadata\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:54\",\"- cidr: fd00:ec2::254/128\",\"IPv6 metadata blocked.\"),\n  R(\"volumes/mounts\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/deployment.yaml:66\",\"- {name: sts-token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true}\",\"Only read-only token/SVID mounts and a memory tmp; no host paths.\"),\n  R(\"host network/socket\",\"not_applicable\",\"k8s/deployment.yaml:33\",\"hostUsers: false\",\"No hostNetwork, hostPath or docker.sock in any pod spec.\"),\n  R(\"credentials\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/deployment.yaml:51\",\"- name: DATABASE_URL\",\"Agent-scoped DB secret; role limited by grants in migrations/001_init.sql:83.\")])\ncheck(\"B08.3\",\"yes\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:8\",\"policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]\",\n \"Isolation is Kubernetes and Cilium network policy and pod security, not prompt or agent code.\",\n counter=\"Searched src/ and prompts/ for host allowlists the model can steer; only output.allowed_link_hosts for reply links (main.py:104), which is not isolation.\",\n rows=[R(\"network isolation\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:8\",\"policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]\",\"Enforced by CNI.\"),\n  R(\"namespace hardening\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/admission.yaml:6\",\"pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted\",\"Pod security enforced at namespace level.\")])\n# ---------- B09\ncheck(\"B09.1\",\"yes\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:32\",\"- toFQDNs:\",\n \"Egress is default-deny with an FQDN and endpoint allowlist enforced by Cilium, with DNS names restricted.\",\n counter=\"Searched for 0.0.0.0/0, wildcard egress and proxy-only controls; none.\",\n rows=[R(\"agent external egress\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:33\",\"- matchName: api.anthropic.com\",\"Only api.anthropic.com and sso.acme.example on 443.\"),\n  R(\"DNS names\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:28\",\"dns:\",\"DNS answers limited to the two names and cluster names.\"),\n  R(\"gateway egress\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:68\",\"egress:\",\"Only named internal peers; no external destination.\")])\ncheck(\"B09.2\",\"no\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:49\",\"- matchLabels: {\\\"k8s:io.kubernetes.pod.namespace\\\": helpdesk, app: helpdesk-mcp}\",\n \"The agent policy allows a direct route to helpdesk-mcp, and gateway_client.py:52-59 uses it for escalate_to_human (tools.yaml:91) when the gateway is unreachable, so policy does not force traffic through the gateway.\")\ncheck(\"B09.3\",\"unknown\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:52\",\"- toCIDR: [169.254.169.254/32, 169.254.170.2/32, 100.100.100.200/32]\",\n \"Agent has no model-steered fetch tool; metadata IPv4/IPv6 denied at the CNI. Redirects and resolved-IP checks and 127.0.0.0/8/::1 blocks are not shown in repo; the Anthropic SDK client handles redirects (not inspected). Searched src/ for follow_redirects and URL fetchers.\")\ncheck(\"B09.4\",\"unknown\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:34\",\"- matchName: api.anthropic.com\",\n \"api.anthropic.com is allowed by domain only; FQDN policy cannot limit account. Restriction to our API key/org (workspace controls) lives outside this repo.\")\ncheck(\"B09.5\",\"unknown\",\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:51\",\"egressDeny:\",\n \"No Hubble, policy audit log or alert route to a named operator exists in this repo; looked in k8s/, config/ and workflows.\")\n# ---------- B10\ncheck(\"B10.1\",\"yes\",\"k8s/deployment.yaml:43\",\"image: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent@${IMAGE_DIGEST}\",\n \"Every image field uses @sha256 or a digest variable stamped by CI with no tag default.\",\n counter=\"Searched for image: in k8s, workflows and Dockerfile; no tags. Helm, compose and Terraform absent.\",\n rows=[R(\"agent image\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/deployment.yaml:43\",\"image: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent@${IMAGE_DIGEST}\",\"Digest from release manifest; empty value yields an invalid reference that admission rejects.\"),\n  R(\"gateway image\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/deployment.yaml:103\",\"image: registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent@${IMAGE_DIGEST}\",\"Same.\"),\n  R(\"cron image\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml:26\",\"image: registry.acme.example/platform/psql@sha256:\",\"Literal digest.\"),\n  R(\"base images\",\"enforced\",\"Dockerfile:8\",\"FROM gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian12:nonroot@sha256:\",\"Final base pinned; build base pinned at Dockerfile:2.\")])\ncheck(\"B10.2\",\"yes\",\"k8s/admission.yaml:48\",\"subject: \\\"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\\\"\",\n \"Kyverno verifyImages pins an exact keyless subject and issuer, no wildcards.\",\n counter=\"Searched admission.yaml for .*, regex, subjectRegExp and unset issuer; none.\",\n rows=[R(\"agent image signature subject\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/admission.yaml:48\",\"subject: \\\"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\\\"\",\"Exact.\"),\n  R(\"agent image issuer\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/admission.yaml:49\",\"issuer: \\\"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\\\"\",\"Exact.\"),\n  R(\"provenance attestor\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/admission.yaml:56\",\"subject: \\\"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\\\"\",\"Exact.\"),\n  R(\"platform images\",\"enforced\",\"k8s/admission.yaml:79\",\"subject: \\\"https://github.com/acme/platform-images/.github/workflows/build.yml@refs/heads/main\\\"\",\"Exact subject; issuer at line 80.\")])\ncheck(\"B10.3\",\"no\",\"k8s/admission.yaml:72\",\"- imageReferences: [\\\"registry.acme.example/platform/*\\\"]\",\n \"Provenance builder, source repo, build type and externalParameters are checked only for the people/ image (lines 51-71); the platform/* rule verifies a signature only, so images such as the psql CronJob image get no provenance conditions.\")\ncheck(\"B10.4\",\"no\",\"k8s/admission.yaml:35\",\"- image: \\\"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\\\"\",\n \"Mode is Enforce and failurePolicy Fail, but the validate rule only needs registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*; an unsigned image from another repo path in that registry matches no verifyImages rule and is allowed. No deny for images matching no policy.\")\ncheck(\"B10.5\",\"yes\",\"release.yml\",\"with: {cosign-release: \\\"v2.6.2\\\"}\".replace(\"release.yml\",\"\") ,\"x\") if False else None\nE\ncd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-r46cle5_/agent && python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\np=\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-brenn-dev-brace/255658ca-f19b-460c-8892-2a477de97733/scratchpad/drv/ans.py\"\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s[:s.index('check(\"B10.5\"')]\ns+='''check(\"B10.5\",\"yes\",\".github/workflows/release.yml:27\",\"with: {cosign-release: \\\\\"v2.6.2\\\\\"}\",\n \"CI pins Cosign v2.6.2, which meets the 2.6.2 minimum.\",\n counter=\"Searched workflows, Dockerfile and manifests for other cosign pins or latest; none. Kyverno's own verifier version is not in this repo.\",\n rows=[R(\"CI cosign pin\",\"enforced\",\".github/workflows/release.yml:27\",\"with: {cosign-release: \\\\\"v2.6.2\\\\\"}\",\"v2.6.2 >= 2.6.2.\"),\n  R(\"Dockerfile/policy-controller\",\"not_applicable\",\"Dockerfile:17\",\"ENTRYPOINT [\\\\\"python3\\\\\"]\",\"No cosign in Dockerfile or charts.\")])\n'''\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"release.yml:27\" /dev/null; sed -n 27p .github/workflows/release.yml"}}}
