{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChG1bswSULkGddyYyQMAx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validator (`--fix --batch … --before-challenges`) reports one problem, an unresolved prescan hit. I skipped prescan hits as instructed, so it's still there. The hit is H008, `src/main.py:106`, tagged B06. It looks harmless: `state.pending_approval` is a response payload, not something the model writes.\n\n| Item | Rating | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity | gap | B06.4 is no. The approval grant is bound to instance, operation, target and args hash, and is consumed atomically. But when the gateway is unreachable, `escalate_to_human` falls back to `direct_route` (`config/tools.yaml:91`, `src/gateway_client.py:52-59`). That skips the gateway's permission and stop-flag recheck at execution. |\n| B07 Execution budgets | gap | B07.2 and B07.4 are no. The resume path makes an uncounted `get_leave_balance` call (`src/agent.py:154`), and the Anthropic client retries once outside the counters (`src/main.py:172`). Tool-rate limits are per-replica, in-memory (`src/gateway.py:48`), with no tenant or fleet rate quota. Spend quotas are checked only at run start, so concurrent runs can overshoot the user cap (up to about $60 against $3). |\n| B08 Environment isolation | likely_pass | Default-deny network policy with named peers, and cloud metadata denied on IPv4 and IPv6. |\n| B09 Egress allowlist | gap | B09.2 is no. The agent's policy allows a direct route to helpdesk-mcp (`k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:49`) around the gateway. B09.3, B09.4 and B09.5 are unknown, because redirect and resolved-IP checks, per-account limits on `api.anthropic.com`, and block alerting aren't visible in the repo. |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image | gap | B10.3 and B10.4 are no. The `platform/*` admission rule (`k8s/admission.yaml:72`) has no provenance conditions. The registry pattern at `:35` lets unsigned images from other repo paths through. |\n\n- **Shared cause:** B06 and B09 share the `direct_route` cause, so each lists the other in `also_affects`.\n- **B06.1 judgement call:** I answered yes, although `approvals.grants` has no separate scope column. I treated the stored operation as fixing the scope, via `config/tools.yaml:60`. Say if you'd rather count that as no.\n- **Not done:** challenges, topology mapping, falsification attempts and step 9 fix details for the gaps, per your instructions.\n- **Side effects:** the skill scripts wrote `agent/brace-prescan.json` and `agent/brace-inventory.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1529,"cache_read_input_tokens":109616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1529},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f14022b-46ce-4936-8598-8b32b34af28b","uuid":"322db2a8-e2b0-4b94-afb0-bd12a8fab375","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:41:15.940Z","request_id":"req_011ChG1bskXNChYrGegboTQh"}
